# OpenAI platform credentials and defaults
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
OPENAI_RESPONSES_MODEL="gpt-5-mini"
OPENAI_VOICE_MODEL="gpt-4o-mini-tts"
OPENAI_VOICE="alloy"

# Where generated transcripts and audio will be written
OUTPUT_DIR="./output"

# Prompts drive the Responses API behaviour. Keep the JSON schema the same.
OPENAI_CONVERT_PROMPT="Extract an audiobook-ready transcript from a PDF and return segmented JSON for text-to-speech.\n\nGoals:\n- Clean, flowing prose in the correct reading order.\n- Segments splitting at natural boundaries.\n- Return the entirety of the text; summarise only when absolutely necessary.\n\nCleaning rules\n- Remove headers, footers, page numbers, footnote markers, and line-wrap hyphenation.\n- Merge lines into paragraphs. Keep chapter and section titles.\n- Omit figure/table labels, decorative glyphs, and non-narrative captions.\n- Normalise punctuation and spacing for TTS. Replace odd ligatures. Fix common OCR errors.\n- Remove non-narrative citations and reference lists unless they are needed to understand the text.\n- If the source has no clear chapters/sections, return one chapter with null titles.\n- Do not include any explanation outside the JSON.\n\nOutput format:\n{\n  \"chapters\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Chapter Title or null\",\n      \"sections\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Section Title or null\",\n          \"segments\": [\n            {\n              \"text\": \"Text segment content.\",\n              \"approx_words\": number of words in this segment\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"

OPENAI_CONDENSE_PROMPT="Summarise this document into concise audiobook-ready text with clear sections and key points. Follow the same JSON schema as the conversion prompt and retain factual fidelity."
